  "local_method": "Each signed run began with an empty private SQLite store, a new browser session, new fictional images and the regular website customer workflow. Tesseract read the uploaded image bytes through a local vision adapter. The second vision review used a scripted response, so the exercise establishes local confirmation behavior only. Deterministic model proposals, stored municipal page bytes, the November 26 CISA directory and fake provider transports were used. Each loopback fake store had one fictional slot to exercise the paid path. The public cap and provider configuration were untouched. The normal issuer resolver, quote guards, case service, clock/feasibility computation and database were used. No order, eligible decision or provider object was inserted for the browser. These runs establish local behavior with those provider inputs. They do not measure production OCR or research-model quality.",
